#!/usr/bin/python3 -I
"""sysmon - lightweight system resource & pressure monitor.

Observes, logs and notifies ONLY. It never kills processes, restarts services,
drops caches or changes any system setting.

Subcommands:
  daemon      run the monitor (normally started by sysmon.service as root)
  notify      desktop notifier (normally started by the sysmon-notify user service)
  status      show the current state (also available as `sysmon-status`)
  history     print recorded samples as a table (post-mortem analysis)
  events      show past state changes / alerts
  snapshots   list diagnostic snapshots
  snapshot    ask the running daemon to take a snapshot now (root)
  selftest    run simulated scenarios through the alert logic (no real load)
  config      validate and print the effective configuration
"""

